#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) parallel whistler-Alfven wave test.
Hall-only: validates the Hall term of the generalized Ohm's law in normalized
CGS units (resistivity and electron-pressure-gradient terms disabled).

Parameters are chosen so that in CODE (normalized) units the ion scales are
O(1) and the ion cyclotron motion is resolved by the timestep:
  Geometry in code units; box Lx = 6.4 d_i. With lNormSI = uNormSI = 1.0e5,
  tNorm = 1 s so TimeMax (s) equals code time; with q/(m c) = 1 for the proton,
  B = Omega_i ~ 1.  With dt = 0.02, dt*Omega_i = 0.02 << 1 so the Hall/whistler
  mode (omega/Omega_i = (k d_i)^2/(1+(k d_i)^2)) is numerically stable.  The
  n=1 mode has omega ~ 0.49 rad/s, period T ~ 12.8 s.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#AVGFIELDB
T                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB

#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

Sub-cycle the B update. The explicit Hall advance is limited by the discrete
grid-scale whistler mode, omega_max * dt_sub < S (S ~ 2.83 for RK4). Because the
compact curl operators (curl_center_to_node / curl_node_to_center) annihilate
the exact Nyquist mode and are far less stiff than the continuum estimate, the
effective omega_max here is ~100/Omega_i, so even dt = 0.02 is within the RK4
limit and nBSubcycle = 1 is stable (verified: the measured whistler frequency
is identical for nBSubcycle in {1,4,8,16,32}). 8 is chosen as a conservative
margin that is 4x cheaper than the previous 32 while still exercising the
sub-cycling machinery.
#BSUBCYCLE
8                       nBSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
1.0439e-8               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
HybridWave

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
100                     dn
-1                      dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
13.0                    TimeMax   ~1 whistler period (n=1 mode)

#RUN
